# Fixed-width subtype store rejects a numeric overflow

Verifies an `int8<mm>[]` element enforces its numeric representation as well as
its unit. `127mm + 1mm` stays a millimeter length but its magnitude `128mm`
does not fit `int8`, so the store is rejected instead of accepting the value
because the unit matches.

>>> source
let a: int8<mm>[] = [127mm]
a[0] = a[0] + 1mm
print(a[0])

<<< stdout

<<< stderr
eck: array element `128mm` cannot be represented as `int8[mm]`

<<< exit
1
